# E-465: Let $N(X,\delta)$ denote the maximum number of points $P_1,\ldots,P_n$ which can be chosen in a circle of radius $X$ such that\[\| \lvert P_i-P_j\rvert \| \geq \delta\]for all $1\leq i<j\leq n$. (Here $\|x\|$ is the distance from $x$ to the nearest integer.) Is it true that, for any $0<\delta<1/2$, we have\[N(X,\delta)=o(X)?\]In fact, is it true that (for any fixed $\delta>0$)\[N(X,\delta)<X^{1/2+o(1)}?\]
